{"baseRefName":"fix/ux-trust-fixes","baseRefOid":"46d5eba5d78c23ca0c978b516f6364b00882b1ca","body":"## Summary\nStacked on #527. Fixes the falsification-tested findings from the interaction-trust audit — every item below was reproduced against the real code path before the fix.\n\n**Queue + download surfaces**\n- Queue overlay labels the unplayed head `▶ next up` instead of `▶ playing` — the overlay has no playback authority and was claiming a live session state\n- Queue list windows around the selection (`getWindowStart`); j/k can no longer move the highlight onto rows clipped below the fold where x/reorder would act invisibly\n- Download manager headers/badges use real `COUNT(*)` totals (`countJobsByStatus`/`countJobs`) instead of LIMIT-capped array lengths; repairable reads move to `listRepairable` (`listFailed` intentionally excludes them), reviving the dead `a` repair sweep + hint; rows hidden by bucket caps get an explicit disclosure row\n\n**Stats surfaces**\n- SQLite buckets use `'localtime'` and the JS side shares `localDayKey`, ending the UTC/local off-by-one for UTC+ users; the heatmap ends at the current week (it previously truncated it) and steps with `setDate`, not `+86_400_000`\n\n**Playback + overlay command routing**\n- `history-entry` results from commands launched during loading/active playback are no longer dropped — queue claims roll back with `handoff-failed` and a visible note explains the refusal\n- `/up-next` `/watch` `/playlists` `/providers` `/image-pane` route through `runRootWorkflowSafely` instead of no-oping\n- Queue overlay Enter without a pending waiter claims + delivers the exact row, rolling back on failed handoff\n\n**Details sheet + palettes + trouble hints**\n- Details overlays retain the option that opened them — `Enter`/`w`/`q`/`d` act on it even after the list highlight drifts\n- Both command palettes dismiss on a successful Enter (previously the resolved palette stayed mounted over the next surface and kept eating its keys)\n- The playing-trouble hint row gates `r`/`⇧F`/`o`/`d` on the same capabilities `resolvePlaybackShellInput` checks\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `apps/cli` unit: 1585 app-shell + 726 domain/download-service pass, 0 fail\n- [x] `packages/storage`: 208 pass, 0 fail\n- [x] Regression tests added: details-sheet option ownership, palette-dismiss-on-Enter (both systems), stats local-day bucketing\n- [x] Golden captures regenerated (downloads ×3, library ×2)\n- [x] `typecheck` / `lint` / `fmt` / `verify:doc-paths` clean; full pre-push gate (26 tasks) green\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * The Up Next view now labels the next title clearly and shows a focused section of long queues, with indicators for titles above and below.\n  * Download management shows job totals and how many jobs aren’t visible in the list.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Browse actions now apply to the title that opened the details sheet, even if the highlighted title changes.\n  * Playback statistics and streaks now follow local calendar dates.\n  * Starting another title during playback now provides feedback instead of leaving a queue claim unresolved.\n  * Playback help shows only available actions.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated keybinding descriptions for stopping playback chains and bookmarking titles.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","files":[{"path":".docs/keybindings.md","additions":2,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".docs/mpv-in-process-reconnect.md","additions":27,"deletions":4,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".github/workflows/ci.yml","additions":20,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/src/app-shell/active-playback-command-dispatcher.ts","additions":53,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/src/app-shell/browse-search-state.ts","additions":4,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/cli/src/app-shell